description:
Several security issues were discovered in the Linux kernel.
An attacker could possibly use these to compromise the system.
This update corrects flaws in the following subsystems:
  - Stream parser;
  - x86 architecture;
  - GPU drivers;
  - HID subsystem;
  - I3C subsystem;
  - MemoryStick subsystem;
  - Network drivers;
  - Ethernet team driver;
  - NVME drivers;
  - S/390 drivers;
  - SCSI subsystem;
  - Greybus lights staging drivers;
  - Realtek RTL8723BS SDIO drivers;
  - Thunderbolt and USB4 drivers;
  - TTY drivers;
  - USB Device Class drivers;
  - USB core drivers;
  - USB Gadget drivers;
  - USB Host Controller drivers;
  - USB Serial drivers;
  - USB Mass Storage drivers;
  - USB Type-C Port Controller Manager driver;
  - TI TPS6598x USB Power Delivery controller driver;
  - Ceph distributed file system;
  - File systems infrastructure;
  - F2FS file system;
  - Network file system (NFS) server daemon;
  - File system notification infrastructure;
  - OCFS2 file system;
  - SMB network file system;
  - Kernel futex primitives;
  - VLANs driver;
  - Netfilter;
  - TCP network protocol;
  - Audit subsystem;
  - BPF subsystem;
  - Perf events;
  - Watch queue notification mechanism;
  - Memory management;
  - Bluetooth subsystem;
  - Ethernet bridge;
  - Networking core;
  - HSR network protocol;
  - IPv4 networking;
  - IPv6 networking;
  - IUCV driver;
  - MAC80211 subsystem;
  - Management Component Transport Protocol (MCTP);
  - Netlink;
  - Open vSwitch;
  - Packet sockets;
  - RDS protocol;
  - Network traffic control;
  - SCTP protocol;
  - SMC sockets;
  - TIPC protocol;
  - TLS protocol;
  - VMware vSockets driver;
  - Wireless networking;
  - AppArmor security module;
  - Key management;
  - ALSA framework;
  - Analog Devices audio codecs;
  - USB sound devices;
